+/*
+ * MGS2_SINKMETER=1: per sink, the peak of what the synthesiser actually
+ * rendered, one line per second.
+ *
+ * With the local dsound the sink transport is now audible (a tone written here
+ * is loud at the speaker), yet MGS2's menu clicks still are not.  That leaves
+ * two possibilities which no amount of listening separates: the SE voice renders
+ * far below audibility, or it never renders into an audible sink at all.  A peak
+ * per second per sink separates them.  Scanning the block is cheap next to
+ * synthesising it; the earlier probes were expensive because they logged and
+ * wrote files per render, which this does not.
